      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Since the complexity, morbidity, and costs of coronary interventions are increased when coronary thrombus is present, identification of the cause of an angiographic filling defect is potentially important. We present a case report and review our experience with a flow artifact that mimicked thrombus (\"pseudothrombus\") in the setting of a severe proximal stenosis in the left circumflex coronary artery."},
